<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador truck strike slows supply of gasoline.</title>
<headline>Ecuador truck strike slows supply of gasoline.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuadorean truck drivers began an indefinite strike on Monday, causing gasoline shortages throughout the country.</p>
<p>Local television showed long lines of cars at petrol stations waiting to reach pumps to refuel.</p>
<p>The truck strike began two days before a general strike called by unions for Wednesday. The job action was called to a protest against President Abdala Bucaram and his government's austerity measures, including price-hikes for public services such as electricity, telephone services and public transport.</p>
<p>The government on Monday said it canceled classes at universities and schools on Monday, Tuesday and Wednesday. Students have been among the most active protestors in recent weeks.</p>
<p>((--Quito Newsroom, 5932 258429))</p>
